module gunbc.fleet_converge_timer


// Arc item 4 (timer / anti-entropy, operator directive 2026-08-08): the steady-state
// enforcement loop is a PER-HOST systemd timer executing the converge circuit against
// the admitted desired revision (gunbc.fleet_main_revision) — never a central cron, an
// SSH star, or a GHA event as steady state. Every firing emits a receipt; a host that
// was offline across a desired-state change converges on return because the timer's
// next firing reads the admitted ref (catch-up is a property of following the ref, plus
// Persistent= for missed calendar firings). This module is the SINGLE authority for the
// unit names, cadence, and unit CONTENT — the emitted files derive from these rows, so
// a hand-edited unit is drift against this authority, not a second truth.
//
// Timer shape is the design doc's Option A (OnCalendar + Persistent=true + jitter):
// Persistent only functions with OnCalendar (systemd ignores it on monotonic timers),
// and calendar catch-up is exactly the offline-host property the arc requires.
//
// THE DEAD SELF-INSTALL RENDERER IS GONE (2026-08-18). What stood here was a SECOND systemd
// renderer for these same two units -- `fleet_converge_service_content`,
// `fleet_converge_timer_content`, `fleet_converge_service_content_self` -- feeding the
// srv2-srv4 self-install route, beside `gunbc.live_deploy.emit`'s
// `emit_fleet_converge_{service,timer}_unit_doc` feeding srv1. Two authorities for one unit,
// which two registered `Scaffold` rows here described and neither removed.
//
// It was not merely duplicated, it had DIVERGED into a correctness fork: this body rendered
// `User=root` and omitted `WorkingDirectory=`, the exact b1 defect the emit side shed when it
// moved to the service user -- a root `ls-remote` in a service-user-owned tree with no workdir
// to run git in.
//
// WHY IT COULD BE DELETED RATHER THAN RECONCILED, which is the whole reason this is a deletion
// and not a migration: its only consumer chain was
// `fleet_converge_timer_install.fleet_timer_self_install_wet` <- `ci_spec`'s
// `gunbc_ci_fleet_timer_install_invoke` <- `ci.yml`, and #8283 deleted `ci.yml`. Measured at
// deletion: `fleet_timer_self_install` appears in neither surviving workflow, and
// `gunbc_ci_fleet_timer_install_invoke` had no consumer but its own `DeclarationRef`. The
// remaining callers were its own two witness files.
//
// The retention reason recorded in `fleet_converge_timer_cadence_retired_note` -- kept "for
// teardown of legacy hosts" -- was NOT realized by any code. `live_deploy` teardown derives
// its unit names from `live_deploy.spec` and never called these functions; the note was prose
// asserting a consumer that did not exist. Deleted with them rather than left standing.
//
// Both `Scaffold` rows declared `dissolves_to: SingleAuthority` bound to `gunbc.live_deploy.emit`.
// `live_deploy.emit` is now that single authority, so this deletion FIRES those dissolutions
// rather than adding any -- the obligations are discharged, not inherited.
//
// WHAT SURVIVES HERE, and why each row is still load-bearing: the two unit NAMES are read by
// `gunbc.fleet_converge_plan`, and the cadence and jitter are read by `gunbc.live_deploy.emit`.
// This module remains the naming and cadence authority; it is no longer a renderer.
data fleet_converge_service_unit_name: String = "ctrl-fleet-converge.service"
data fleet_converge_timer_unit_name: String = "ctrl-fleet-converge.timer"
data fleet_converge_timer_on_calendar: String = "*:0/15"
data fleet_converge_timer_randomized_delay: std.measure.Second = std.measure.second(count: 90)
